> Is there any adventage to using the fireproofed boots of water walking
> over levitation? Should I even bring them?

My ideas -

Being unburdened is necessary.  Drop the useless stuff.  As soon as you
hit 18/** strength you can drop the tinning kit, saving you lots of
weight.

Armor is fine, but forget all those boots and wish for fixed speed
boots.  Charge them up to +5.  Stash your water-walking boots / lev
boots in case you need them later.  A ring of levitation is the best
way to fly.

Get rid of the protection ring.  You AC is very good already, the
benefit you get from it is almost negligable now.  ALWAYS wear the ring
of free action.  The other ring finger should swap among (a) slow
digestion, (b) levitation, (c) conflict as needed.

> I am using body armour(GDSM), I never miss when I attack with hands. Am
> I losing damage by using armour? Is it worth it to wear body armour at
> this point(it sure seems to be)?

Maybe a Monk expert can help, but the Eyes provide you with magic
protection so you could dump the armor.    But if you're hitting
everything all the time now, why not wear it?  I think it only
penalizes your to-hit, not damage.  I would carry a backup anti-magic
device.

> What should I do with my 4 wishes? (I have already used wishes so not
> going for conduct)

Speed boots should be #1.  I don't see Charm Monster and a magic
whistle in there, that is a key strategy  for non-combat characters.

> I think I may need more magic markers, and mabye another wand of death.
> Am I missing anything that I need?

Charging scrolls and/or more markers would be good, but you have little
else to charge up.

> I understand that after you get the amulet, you get your items randomly
> cursed, so you need to have things pre blessed and to have lots of holy
> water. If I carry many light useless items, will they absorb some of
> the curse attacks?

Yes, bless your key items.  Especially your gloves, since if they get
cursed you cannot change rings.

Keep a bunch of blessed remove curse scrolls in your bag, and keep your
Remove Curse spell learned.  I think you have enough holy water.  All
that water is actually quite heavy.

